invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
reason: state_finish reduces the k words of the last product's power and
  drops the word above them, so a power at or above 2^(64k), which a
  prime close to 2^(64k) leaves, comes out as the power less 2^(64k) and
  not less the prime. bin/rsa_ifma_sign_model_test hands state_finish
  such powers under a prime of all ones and requires them reduced below
  it.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_reduce_once_with_top(o, words, words[mod->words], mod);
--- new
    rsa_mont64_reduce_once(o, words, mod);
